# Scene
trueqbit with Claude (Opus 5.5), 2026-11-20/21: the symbol-level reading
of the runtime layer (context_switch.h, fiber.h, io_operation.h,
io_uring_engine.h, scheduler.h, io_context.h, io_pool.h): does each
doc-comment say what its symbol is and does, does each symbol's purpose
hold. The P+I round of #1524 had checked only file to symbol.

# Decided
- trueqbit: Claude's leans and routing, except scheduler.h. #1630 got
  fire_and_forget's second user (async_io_context's `detached` was a
  copy) and result_box::invoke() (one try block held twice). #1633,
  new, stacked between #1630 and #1631: schedule() and worker() removed,
  resume_here() private. #1631: the doc-comment points.
- trueqbit: scheduler.h loses nothing; its members follow common
  designs of such loops ("drawn from generally available sources").
  What it holds unused is flagged in the last review step instead.
- "Realizes" stays where a contract stands behind it (async_task and
  fire_and_forget realize the language's coroutine protocol), and goes
  from fiber, io_uring_engine, scheduler and async_io_context.

# Discussed
- pre-commit.sh exits 0 before every commit; the amalgamation's code
  changes only where the refactors mean it to. Not compiled.

